==Background==
[[File:BB28 Promo Logo.jpg|thumb|200px|Promotional Logo]]
[[File:BB 1000th Logo.jpg|thumb|250px|1000th Episode Logo]]
===Development===
Once again, this season was revealed by production ahead of an official renewal announcement from CBS, when they updated their casting website on August 1, 2025 during ''[[Big Brother 27 (US)]]''.

On May 13, 2026, it was announced that the season would have a 90-minute premiere on Thursday, July 9, 2026, followed by another 90-minute episode the next Sunday. The traditional Sunday, Wednesday, Thursday episode schedule returned, with all episodes airing at 8 PM throughout the season. The 90-minute Wednesday episodes returned for this season, while the Sunday and Thursday episodes would remain at an hour length following the premiere week. This season marked the 1000th episode of ''Big Brother US'', a primetime television first, and featured the most programming hours in the show's history. It was also announced that the companion show, ''[[Big Brother: Unlocked]]'', would return for its [[Big Brother: Unlocked/Season 2|second season]], airing every other Friday at 8 PM starting on July 10.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.paramountpressexpress.com/cbs-entertainment/shows/big-brother/releases/?view=112872-big-brother-turns-up-the-heat-with-its-biggest-season-yet-premiering-thursday-july-9-with-a-90-minute-episode|title=“BIG BROTHER” TURNS UP THE HEAT WITH ITS BIGGEST SEASON YET, PREMIERING THURSDAY, JULY 9 WITH A 90-MINUTE EPISODE|publisher=Paramount Press Express|date=13 May 2026}}</ref>
===Canadian Viewership Changes===
On May 26, 2026, it was announced that this season would be the last one to air on [[Global]] in Canada. Global was the home of ''[[Big Brother U.S. (franchise)|Big Brother US]]'' in Canada since its debut, and aired [[Big Brother Canada (franchise)|Canada's own ''Big Brother'' franchise]] from [[Big Brother Canada 3|2014]] to [[Big Brother Canada 12|2024]], after picking it up from sister channel [[Slice]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://globalnews.ca/news/11863358/big-brother-season-28-last-to-air-on-global/|title=Global announces upcoming season of ‘Big Brother’ will be last to air on network|archivedate=27 May 2026|last=Scott|first=Katie|date=27 May 2026|publisher=Global News|accessdate=26 May 2026|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260528034953/https://globalnews.ca/news/11863358/big-brother-season-28-last-to-air-on-global/}}</ref> On June 4, 2026, it was later announced that future seasons would air on [[wikipedia:CTV Television Network|CTV]], following [[wikipedia:Bell Media|Bell Media's]] acquisition of ''[[Big Brother Canada (franchise)|Big Brother Canada]]''.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bellmedia.ca/the-lede/press/bell-media-becomes-head-of-household-with-order-of-big-brother-canada-for-crave-and-ctv-and-acquisition-of-future-seasons-of-big-brother-usa-beginning-in-2027/|title=Bell Media Becomes Head of Household with Order of BIG BROTHER CANADA for Crave and CTV and Acquisition of Future Seasons of BIG BROTHER USA, Beginning in 2027|publisher=Bell Media|date=4 June 2026|accessdate=4 June 2026}}</ref>
