===Unlocked Changes===
[[File:Jerry O'Connell Big Brother Host.jpg|thumb|right|Jerry O'Connell's Official Press Photo]]
On June 30, 2026, CBS announced that actor [[Jerry O'Connell]] would join the [[Big Brother: Unlocked/Season 2|second season]] of ''[[Big Brother: Unlocked]]'' alongside returning hosts and former winners [[Derrick Levasseur]] and [[Taylor Hale]] from the [[Big Brother: Unlocked/Season 1|first season]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.paramountpressexpress.com/cbs-entertainment/shows/big-brother/releases/?view=113009-jerry-oconnell-joins-big-brother-unlocked-as-celebrity-panelist-alongside-returning-winners-taylor-hale-and-derrick-levasseur|title=JERRY O’CONNELL JOINS “BIG BROTHER: UNLOCKED” AS CELEBRITY PANELIST ALONGSIDE RETURNING WINNERS TAYLOR HALE AND DERRICK LEVASSEUR|author=Paramount Press Express|date=30 June 2026|accessdate=30 June 2026}}</ref> O'Connell returns to the franchise after appearing on the second episode of ''Unlocked'' in season 1.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.imdb.com/title/tt37613759/|title=Big Brother: Unlocked #2|publisher=imdb|accessdate=30 June 2026}}</ref> Prior to that, O'Connell was brought in last minute to guest host the Week 8 Eviction in ''[[Big Brother 26 (US)]]'' after it was announced that [[Julie Chen-Moonves]] was quarantining from a COVID infection.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://parade.com/tv/big-brother-26-julie-chen-moonves-covid-absence-jerry-oconnell|title=Why is Julie Chen Moonves Missing from Tonight's 'Big Brother 26' Eviction Episode?|first=Mike|last=Bloom|date=24 September 2024|accessdate=30 June 2026}}</ref>

In the official release, O'Connell stated, "''Big Brother'' is my summer and rolls into my fall too. I’m already watching on Wednesdays, Thursdays and Sundays, so the fact that CBS is now paying me to do it is kind of amazing. It’s an absolute honor to sit next to Derrick – ‘Champ,’ as I call him – and Taylor, who is my all-time favorite ''Big Brother'' winner (sorry, [[Jag Bains|Jag]]). This is what we call in showbiz a dream gig. I’ll do my best to be the voice of the fans, but as Julie says, expect the unexpected. And most importantly, remember to love one another. I’m soooo excited to join the ''Big Brother'' fam!"

The first episode of the sideshow would go on to premiere on July 10th, the night after the premiere.

Unlike the previous season, ''Unlocked'' now featured a live audience for tapings and included voting aspects that would change the game.
===House Reveal===
On July 1st, 2026, CBS released the official house for the first time as the "Time Trip" theme, in which was leaked earlier via the Chinese Promotional Leak earlier in the preseason.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://parade.com/tv/big-brother-28-time-travel-theme-house-pictures-video|title=CBS Announces ‘Big Brother 28’s ‘Time Trip’ Theme: See First-Look House Photos|first=Mike|last=Bloom|date=1 July 2026|accessdate=1 July 2026|publisher=Parade}}</ref><ref name="China Leak"/> 

The theme has centered around time travel as the franchise prepares for it's landmarked 1,000 episode that will air during the season. The house has, "turning time into the ultimate twist. Houseguests will enter a world where rooms, relics and competitions transport them across moments in time, while early twists shake up the game from the start. Inspired by decades like the ’80s and Y2K, new powers and challenges can disrupt strategy and alliances."<ref name="Paramount House PR">{{Cite web|url=https://www.paramountpressexpress.com/cbs-entertainment/shows/big-brother/releases/?view=113016-first-look-big-brother-time-trip-warps-houseguests-through-the-past-present-and-future-in-a-season-of-endless-possibilities|title=FIRST LOOK: “BIG BROTHER: TIME TRIP” WARPS HOUSEGUESTS THROUGH THE PAST, PRESENT AND FUTURE IN A SEASON OF ENDLESS POSSIBILITIES|author=Paramount Press Express|date=1 July 2026|accessdate=1 July 2026}}</ref>

