According to the official press release, the house highlights include:
*'''Time-Bending Entryway:''' Houseguests are greeted by a striking faux neon sign and a dizzying array of clocks, immediately setting the tone: time is fractured, unpredictable and constantly in motion.
*'''Living Room of Eras:''' 17-foot gothic windows glow against oxblood stone walls, blending classic and industrial design alongside relics from across history, from a triceratops skull to royal crown jewels – a reminder that anything from any era could shape the game.
*'''Nostalgic Trophies:''' A 1940s jukebox and an ’80s transparent phone highlight a surreal mix of decades, celebrating nostalgia as past, present and future collide inside the BB house.
*'''Relic Lab Hallway:''' The iconic time laser returns alongside quirky failed inventions including a pogo stick, keytar and more, all displayed as relics of past experiments.
*'''Clockwork Bathroom:''' Gears and intricate mechanical details surround Houseguests, while sub-atomic-inspired lighting fixtures create a visually stunning otherworldly atmosphere.
*'''The Artifact Bedroom:''' Housing five houseguests, this artifact-filled room features two mysterious doorways – one to the past, one to the future.
*'''Futuristic Sleep Pods Room:''' A sleek retreat with pod beds, organic ladders and nebula visuals offers a calm, futuristic escape from the chaos of the game.
*'''Upstairs Lounge:''' Vintage tech lines the shelves. Massive arched windows overlooking the living room make it a prime vantage point for eavesdropping, while the custom-built sofa is perfectly suited for both strategizing and showmancing.
*'''Time-Lapse Gym:''' Walls wrapped in time-lapse photography create the illusion of motion and progression, energizing Houseguests as they work out and reset.
*'''Clock Tower Feature:''' Tying the entire house together, a dramatic clock tower crowns the space, a symbolic reminder that in this game, time is always ticking … but never predictable.<ref name="Paramount House PR"/>

Earlier in the week, [[Julie Chen-Moonves]] led journalists on a tour inside of the house.
===Potential Returning Aspects===
[[File:US 28 House 1.png|thumb|right|200px|Julie in the entrance way for the season's house.<br><small>Matthew Taplinger/CBS</small>]]
As the season is a theme of a blast to the past, Julie hinted as some previous season aspects could be returning to the ''Big Brother'' game. 

In a quote to [[wikipedia:Men%27s_Journal|Men's Journal]] reporter Sharon Tharp, she stated, "time travel, so that could go forward or backwards, and that will play into some of the competitions. Maybe we’ll do the new twist, which is you love that competition in Season 4, but they have to be in, like, I don’t know, surrounded by dinosaurs, who knows."<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.mensjournal.com/entertainment/julie-chen-moonves-hints-controversial-reality-tv-veterans-big-brother-28-cast|title=Julie Chen Moonves Hints ‘Controversial’ Reality TV Veterans Will Be Factored Into ‘Big Brother 28’|first=Sharon|last=Tharp|date=1 July 2026|accessdate=1 July 2026|publisher=Men's Journal}}</ref>

Julie would then state that "Controversial people will be factored in." When asked who, and the possibility of which other possible reality show could be featured, she stated, "If you’re a Big Brother fan, you’ll be like, ‘Aha!’ And I think a lot of people will be like, ‘Yes!’ And I think some people [will be] like, ‘What?’ But it’s good TV. And if you love reality television beyond Big Brother…you’ll be excited as well."
===Big Brother Broveal===
[[File:BB Broveal.jpg|thumb|right|250px|''Big Brother: Broveal'' logo]]
On July 6, 2026, CBS announced the ''Big Brother: Broveal'', a YouTube livestream that will be hosted by Julie as she reveals the cast and dives deeper into the theme, the house and the twists. Following this inaugural stream, the YouTube channel will be used to showcase Live Feeds for free for limited periods following the conclusion of each episode, including ''Unlocked''. Live Feeds will still be hosted with full access for Pluto TV and Paramount+ subscribers.<ref name="Paramount Broveal PR"> {{Cite web|url=https://www.paramountpressexpress.com/cbs-entertainment/shows/big-brother/releases/?view=113031-big-brother-debuts-two-new-live-fan-experiences-available-on-its-official-youtube-channel|title=“BIG BROTHER” DEBUTS TWO NEW LIVE FAN EXPERIENCES AVAILABLE ON ITS OFFICIAL YOUTUBE CHANNELS|author=Paramount Press Express|date=6 July 2026|accessdate=6 July 2026}}</ref>

The reveal was set as a live premiere on YouTube on July 6th to air on July 7th.<ref>@BBigBrotherBuzz. “[https://x.com/BBigBrotherBuzz/status/2074240366165860825 The waiting room is LIVE! CBS has officially opened the YouTube waiting room for tomorrow’s #BB28 “Big Brother: Broveal” cast reveal livestream! Set a reminder now so you don’t miss the reveal at 12:00 PM ET tomorrow!  #BigBrother #BigBrotherBuzz]” X, 6 July 2026. Retrieved 7 July 2026</ref> However, an hour before it was to go live, it was taken offline in order to, according to [https://www.hamsterwatch.com/ Hamsterwatch], swap out a houseguest.<ref>@BBigBrotherBuzz. “[https://x.com/BBigBrotherBuzz/status/2074513806198268326 The #BB28 Broveal waiting room has been taken down. #BigBrother #BigBrotherBuzz]” X, 7 July 2026. Retrieved 7 July 2026</ref><ref name="Hamsterwatch Cast Reveal">@hamsterwatch.com‬. “[https://bsky.app/profile/hamsterwatch.com/post/3mq2vxn7ank2p happy Day 1! happy move-in! happy Broveal! to all who celebrate! #bb28 a slight revision to my alphabet soup - as always, it's not necessarily accurate, correct, or complete but we're now at  A A B C D D H J K L L L M M R R T]” Bsky, 7 July 2026. Retrieved 7 July 2026</ref>

In a post by Hamsterwatch, the letters "A A B C D D H J K L L L M M R R T" were revealed to be the initials of the seventeen houseguests that would be entering the house.<ref name="Hamsterwatch Cast Reveal"/> When the cast was revealed, 13 initials would go on to match the 14 houseguests revealed by CBS.<ref name="Cast Reveal PR"/> It was then discovered that [[Levi Banks]] was supposed to be the fourteenth houseguest, but was replaced in the final moments by [[Yash Patel]] after it was revealed in a preseason article that was not adjusted before the reveal.<ref name="Levi Twitter Find">@brendalowesveto‬. “[https://bsky.app/profile/hamsterwatch.com/post/3mq2vxn7ank2p who tf is this???? #BB28]” X, 7 July 2026. Retrieved 8 July 2026</ref><ref name="Levi Reveal Men's Joural">{{Cite web|last=Tharp|first=Sharon|date=7 July 2026|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260707164916/https://www.mensjournal.com/entertainment/big-brother-season-28-cast-meet-houseguests-photos-bios|accessdate=8 July 2026|title=(Wayback Machine) ‘Big Brother’ Season 28 Cast Revealed: Meet the New Houseguests}}</ref>

That would be the explanation for the additional "L" and no "Y".

Shortly after the reveal, the official Paramount press site released a press release stating that, "Additional surprise Houseguests will be revealed on air," signifying that more houseguests would be revealed on the premiere episode.<ref name="Cast Reveal PR"> {{Cite web|url=https://www.paramountpressexpress.com/cbs-entertainment/shows/big-brother/releases/?view=113033-big-brother-introduces-a-new-cast-of-houseguests-to-a-game-where-the-past-present-and-future-collide|title=“BIG BROTHER” INTRODUCES A NEW CAST OF HOUSEGUESTS TO A GAME WHERE THE PAST, PRESENT AND FUTURE COLLIDE|author=Paramount Press Express|date=7 July 2026|accessdate=7 July 2026|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260707171622/https://www.paramountpressexpress.com/cbs-entertainment/shows/big-brother/releases/?view=113033-big-brother-introduces-a-new-cast-of-houseguests-to-a-game-where-the-past-present-and-future-collide|archivedate=7 July 2026}}</ref> 
====Additional Players Revealed====
Three hours after the initial cast release, ''[[wikipedia:Entertainment Weekly|Entertainment Weekly's]]'' [https://x.com/DaltonRoss Dalton Ross] revealed that ''Survivor'' contestants would be included in the season's cast. In an exclusive announcement for ''Entertainment Weekly'', former ''[[w:c:survivor:Survivor: Edge of Extinction|Survivor: Edge of Extinction]]'' and ''[[w:c:survivor:Survivor 50: In the Hands of the Fans|Survivor 50: In the Hands of the Fans]]'' contestant [[Rick Devens]] would be joining the cast.<ref name="Devens EW Reveal">{{Cite web|url=https://ew.com/survivor-star-rick-devens-to-compete-on-big-brother-exclusive-12013019|title=Survivor star Rick Devens to compete on Big Brother season 28 (exclusive)|last=Ross|first=Dalton|date=7 July 2026|accessdate=8 July 2026|archivedate=8 July 2026|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260708053112/https://ew.com/survivor-star-rick-devens-to-compete-on-big-brother-exclusive-12013019}}</ref>

In the same article, it stated "And Devens is not the only former Survivor competitor that will be part of the new cast, as EW has learned that a second former castaway will also be vying for ''Big Brother’s'' $750,000 prize. The identity of that second player has yet to be revealed." 

As well as the Rick Devens speculation, former ''[[w:c:survivor:Survivor 45|Survivor 45]]'' winner and fellow ''Survivor 50: In the Hands of the Fans'' competitor [[Dee Valladares]] was leaked online by various social media accounts.<ref>@Realitytv__fan “[https://x.com/Realitytv__fan/status/2074569761514488167 Survivor castaway Rick Devens will be part of the cast of Big Brother 28, Entertainment Weekly has revealed. Survivor winner Dee Valladares will also be on the cast. #BB28]” X, 7 July 2026. Retrieved 8 July 2026</ref><ref name="Devens Inside Survivor Reveal">{{Cite web|url=https://insidesurvivor.com/two-survivor-50-players-to-compete-on-big-brother-28-61640|title=Two Survivor 50 Players to Compete on Big Brother 28|last=Holmes|first=Martin|date=7 July 2026|accessdate=8 July 2026|archivedate=8 July 2026|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260708054224/https://insidesurvivor.com/two-survivor-50-players-to-compete-on-big-brother-28-61640}}</ref> However, it would be revealed that Dee's participation would not be revealed until the first episode of ''Big Brother: Unlocked''.<ref name="Angela Men's Journal Reveal">{{Cite web|url=https://www.mensjournal.com/entertainment/big-brother-angela-murray-season-28-survivor-players-exclusive|title=‘Big Brother’ Alum Angela Murray Joins Season 28 Alongside Two ‘Survivor’ Players (Exclusive)|last=Tharp|first=Sharon|date=7 July 2026|accessdate=8 July 2026|archivedate=8 July 2026|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260708054601/https://www.mensjournal.com/entertainment/big-brother-angela-murray-season-28-survivor-players-exclusive}}</ref>

One hour later, Sharon Tharp exclusively revealed that [[Angela Murray]] from ''[[Big Brother 26 (US)]]'' would be the sole ''Big Brother'' returnee.<ref name="Angela Men's Journal Reveal"/> By returning, season 28 becomes the second season in a row that a single ''Big Brother'' alum would return to play alongside new houseguests.
===Time Travel Theme===
[[File:Enzo US 28 Appearance.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Enzo's "Meow Meow Enterprises" behind this season's Time Travel theme]]
The theme for the season was revealed to be time travel. Throughout the season, the houseguests would be traveling through time to compete in competitions and twists.

On premiere night, it was revealed that [[Enzo Palumbo]] from ''[[Big Brother 12 (US)]]'' & ''[[Big Brother 22 (US)]]'' was behind the dining room "time machine" with his "company" "Meow Meow Enterprises"

According to Enzo, the multi-verse laser from ''[[Big Brother 25 (US)]]'' & ''[[Big Brother: Reindeer Games]]'' that was broken by former houseguests [[Britney Haynes]], [[Danielle Reyes]] & [[Frankie Grande]] gave him the idea for time travel, that led to this season's twist format.
===Mickey Lee Tribute===
[[File:BB28 Mickey Memorial.png|thumb|right|200px|Titlecard tribute in the opening moments of the season.]]
