==Twists==
*'''[[Second Chance Challenge|BB Block Buster]]:''' Returning for a third season in a row, the BB Block Buster forces the Head of Household to nominate three houseguests for eviction. Then on eviction night, the three nominated houseguests will have a last chance opportunity to save themselves.<ref name="Blockbuster Returns">{{Cite web|url=https://parade.com/tv/julie-chen-moonves-loved-white-locust-twist-bb-blockbuster-season-27-theme|title=Julie Chen Moonves Defends Rachel Reilly’s Controversial ‘Big Brother’ Exit: ‘It Wasn’t Fair. Neither Is Life.’|last=Bloom|first=Mike|date=2 July 2026|accessdate=8 July 2026|archivedate=8 July 2026|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260708055811/https://parade.com/tv/julie-chen-moonves-loved-white-locust-twist-bb-blockbuster-season-27-theme}}</ref>
*'''[[Immunity Competition|Premiere Night Safety]]:''' On premiere night, the fourteen new houseguests would not be eligible for the first Head of Household. As a result, the houseguests would compete for safety from the first eviction. After a qualifying competition, twelve of the fourteen would be divided into three groups of four in which one would win immunity for the week. The winner of each competition would unleash a "Reality Icon" into the game.
*'''Additional Houseguests:''' After each competition on premiere night, a "Reality Icon" would then enter the game after receiving a letter telling them to show up to the ''Big Brother'' House in 2026. The icons were revealed as [[Returning Players|former ''Big Brother'' houseguest]] [[Angela Murray]] from ''[[Big Brother 26 (US)]]'', alongside ''[[w:c:survivor:Survivor (U.S.)|Survivor]]'' alumni [[Rick Devens]] and [[Dee Valladares]].<ref name="Devens EW Reveal"/><ref name="Devens Inside Survivor Reveal"/><ref name="Angela Men's Journal Reveal"/>
**'''Fake Houseguest:''' In was initially teased that former winner [[Rachel Reilly]] would enter the game as the seventeenth houseguest for the second consecutive season, however, it would be revealed that she was not actually playing and another icon would be taking her spot in the game. This icon was then revealed to be Dee.
[[File:US 28 Time Capsule Set.png|thumb|right|350px|A look inside the Time Capsule from above.]]
*'''BB Time Capsule''': During the first week, a fan vote opened up giving America the option to send a houseguest into the BB Time Capsule, giving them the chance to win a power or suffer a punishment from a prior season. Beginning in Week 2 and going until Week 7, the houseguest who wins the vote will enter the Time Capsule and compete to try and earn a power, or fail and receive a punishment. There will be six different powers and punishments up for grabs. Once a houseguest is voted into the Time Capsule, they are ineligible to go in again, win or lose.
*'''Year 1000 Double Eviction:''' To celebrate 1,000 episodes, the houseguests faced a new twist during the start of Week 8, with no HoH, PoV, or Block Buster, but still ending with someone getting sent home before the next live show, leaving the Final 9 houseguests to make up the jury phase.
**'''Stone of Safety:''' The houseguests will be facing off in four competitions. The winner of each competition will become safe for the night and can select one other person to save alongside them. The winner and the person they save are ineligible to compete in the rest of the competitions.
**'''Stone of Sacrifice:''' The first houseguest who wins safety must sacrifice two houseguests, forcing them to face off in the next round of competitions. The winner then earns safety for themselves and one other person, and also chooses the next person (or people) to go against the person that was left behind. The winner of the fourth and final competition will then have the sole vote to evict between the remaining houseguests who are not safe.
*'''[[Temptation Competition|Pharaoh's Curse]]:''' The Final 5 houseguests were given the chance to have everyone get $1,000, but they would be each tempted with their own button. The first person to push that button, if anyone, would earn $10,000 for themselves, leaving everyone else with nothing. If no one pushes the button, everyone keeps their $1,000. However, unbeknownst to the houseguests, pushing the button would subsequently unleash a curse on the house, an extra "Egyptian Eviction" to determine 5th place in the middle of the week. During the eviction, the houseguests would publicly cast their votes by destroying an artifact belonging to one of the nominees.

